rsz: experiment, a worst-slack query every hundred passes and nothing else

Study experiment, not a fix. On riscv32i grt the stall-exit arm and the
control diverge from the first endpoint, before any termination rule
could fire; the only code that runs differently before pass 200 is an
extra sta::worstSlack query at pass 100. This binary adds only that
query. If it reproduces the closure, the legacy loop is acting on stale
timing and the win is a bug, not a policy.

diff --git a/src/rsz/src/policy/SetupLegacyBase.cc b/src/rsz/src/policy/SetupLegacyBase.cc
index 859f085353..b1ff6d73e6 100644
--- a/src/rsz/src/policy/SetupLegacyBase.cc
+++ b/src/rsz/src/policy/SetupLegacyBase.cc
@@ -956,6 +956,13 @@ bool SetupLegacyBase::terminateProgress(const int iteration,
     }
     float inc_fix_rate = (prev_tns - curr_tns) / initial_tns;
     prev_tns = curr_tns;
+    {
+      // Experiment: does asking STA for the worst slack here, and doing
+      // nothing with the answer, change what the optimizer does next?
+      sta::Slack probe_wns;
+      sta::Vertex* probe_vertex = nullptr;
+      sta_->worstSlack(max_, probe_wns, probe_vertex);
+    }
     if (iteration > 1000 && inc_fix_rate < fix_rate_threshold) {
       debugPrint(logger_,
